  "name": "SCRUB TYPHUS (ORIENTIA TSUTSUGAMUSHI) DETECTION QUALITATIVE PCR",
  "code": "2509",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; height: 100.125px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 33.2867%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.2867%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.2867%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.375px;\">\n<td>&nbsp;Result</td>\n<td>Remarks&nbsp;</td>\n<td>Conclusion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.375px;\">\n<td>Positive</td>\n<td>Indicates the presence of Orientia tsutsugamushi DNA in the&nbsp;given sample</td>\n<td>&nbsp;Confirming the presence of Scrub Typhus disease</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 33.375px;\">\n<td>&nbsp;Negative</td>\n<td>Indicates the absence of Orientia tsutsugamushi DNA in the&nbsp;given sample</td>\n<td>Confirming the absence of Scrub Typhus&nbsp;disease</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Indeterminate</td>\n<td>&nbsp;Indicates that inhibitors were detected in the provided sample</td>\n<td>Recommended to repeat with a fresh&nbsp;sample</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Note:<br>1. Positive result indicates the presence of Orientia tsutsugamushi DNA in the given sample by targeting highly<br>conserved sequence (HtrA).<br>2. Negative result indicates absence of Orientia tsutsugamushi DNA and hence negative for Scrub typhus disease.<br>3. False-positive outcome in a PCR test for Scrub Typhus can occur due to contamination during specimen collection,<br>processing or testing, or cross -reactivity of the PCR test's primers or probes with DNA from other bacteria or viruses<br>that are similar to Orientia tsutsugamushi.<br>4. False-negative outcome in a PCR test for Scrub Typhus implies that the test was unable to identify the existence of<br>Orientia tsutsugamushi DNA in the sample. This can happen due to various reasons, such as a low bacterial count,<br>early stages of infection, antibiotic treatment, an inadequate specimen, mutations, or the presence of inhibitors.</p>",
